From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:05:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: 320 dpi

The Robin's 5.2-inch 1080p panel is 424 dpi; the upstream 480 renders everything a size too
large on a screen this small. 320 reports the 1080x1920 panel as 540 dp wide, which is the
room dense layouts need, and it is the one value here that is an exact resource bucket:
at 320 the panel is xhdpi, so bitmaps land 1:1 instead of being scaled up from xhdpi as
they are at 360, 378 or 420. It stays under the sw600dp breakpoint, so apps do not switch
to tablet layouts. The Display Size ladder SettingsLib builds from
display_density_min_scale (70%) and _min_scale_interval (9%) recomputes around it as
224 / 256 / 288 / 320 and upwards, so anyone who finds it small can move it in Settings.

TARGET_RECOVERY_DENSITY is pinned because recovery derives its asset bucket from
TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY, and build/make/core/Makefile splits xxhdpi at >= 400. Without the
pin, 320 would silently drop recovery to xhdpi artwork; the panel itself has not changed.
---
 BoardConfig.mk | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/BoardConfig.mk b/BoardConfig.mk
index 5593a0f..ad33875 100644
--- a/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -81,7 +81,8 @@ TARGET_VNDK_USE_CORE_VARIANT := true
 WITH_DEXPREOPT_DEBUG_INFO := false
 
 # Display
-TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY := 480
+TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY := 320
+TARGET_RECOVERY_DENSITY := xxhdpi
 TARGET_USES_ION := true
 
 # Encryption
